<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">A release is ready, but one distribution route lacks the identity and package proof required for that route. A signing task has become an operational ownership gap.</p>

<!-- @before Distribution Inventory :: guide -->
### Keep the policy attached to the channel

The source’s dated September 2026 rollout covers specified regions and certified Android devices; broader expansion is planned. Verify the current official scope, account workflow and any applicable exceptions for each channel. Do not infer that every distributor uses the same console process. [Current verification requirements](https://developer.android.com/developer-verification).

<!-- @before Signing-Key Proof and Operations :: staff -->
### Name the owner who can prove the package

Maintain package names, signing identities, account access, delegated authority and recovery contacts together. A release deadline is a poor time to discover that the only person able to complete proof is unavailable.

<!-- @before Signing-Key Proof and Operations :: visual -->
### Registration joins publisher, package and signing proof

```mermaid
flowchart TB
 c["Distribution channel Applicable current requirements"]
 i["Publisher identity Verified account owner"]
 p["Package registration Application identity"]
 k["Signing-key proof Authorized custody"]
 o["Release owner Access and recovery"]
 c -->|"determine required workflow"| o
 i -->|"register under verified owner"| p
 k -->|"prove package authority"| p
 o -->|"maintain account access"| i
 o -->|"maintain proof capability"| k
```

Inventory each channel against its current applicable verification workflow. The diagram is an ownership checklist, not an invented enforcement schedule.
